From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hero Siege Offline Toolkit <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Leave the ExecuteIt hook out by design, and say so

Why: Hero Siege (GameMaker YYC x64) runs with a YYToolkit whose ExecuteIt detour was removed, but nothing showed it. CreateCallback(EVENT_OBJECT_CALL) still returned AURIE_SUCCESS for a callback that could never fire, YYToolkit.log read the same with the hook on or off, and a game patch that broke the ExecuteIt byte pattern would have stopped the whole toolkit from loading for an address that only labels crash-report frames. This makes the off state a named build switch (YYTK_HOOK_EXECUTEIT, default 0, in the DLL-private ObjectCallGate.hpp), a runtime flag raised only beside a successful MmCreateHook, one init log line, and an AURIE_UNAVAILABLE refusal whose logging stops after 8 lines.

Evidence: HkExecuteIt only dispatches EVENT_OBJECT_CALL (Hooks.cpp:122-156) and that event is dispatched nowhere else; m_CodeExecute has one reader, GmResolveGameSymbolFromAddress (Generic.cpp:206); upstream CreateCallback validates no trigger (Interface.cpp:1307-1327). No plugin in the toolkit registers EVENT_OBJECT_CALL (ForgePact registers EVENT_FRAME only). Project notes (hub AGENTS.md, "Don't Suspend the Game's Own Runtime") record the hook crash-looping on Season 10; ForgePact/docs/S10-special-content-notes.md section "YYToolkit'in olumcul hatasi BIZDEN DEGIL" records the blamed error occurring with the hook removed. Built here: Release x64 with 0 errors and no new warnings, in both YYTK_HOOK_EXECUTEIT=0 and =1; the =0 DLL contains all four log markers and the =1 DLL does not contain the "NOT installed" line; hs-tests/ObjectCallGateTest.cpp passes 45 checks, and fails 7 of them when the limiter is mutated to an off-by-one. NOT verified: anything in the running game - the init line, the refusal lines and the AURIE_UNAVAILABLE return were never observed live. NOT measured: whether the hook is harmful on Season 10 (not observed either way), and what the detour costs per call. ASSUMED: CreateCallback can be reached from more than one thread, which is why the counter is atomic; the callback list itself stays unguarded as it is upstream.

Fails-safe: The flag defaults to false and only a successful MmCreateHook raises it, so every failure mode refuses the registration instead of accepting a dead callback. A failed ExecuteIt lookup no longer aborts stage 1: m_CodeExecute stays nullptr and the init line says that crash-report frames may be mislabelled Code_Execute. If the owner of a routine cannot be resolved the refusal line says <unknown>; the plugin-supplied AurieModule pointer is never dereferenced. The refusal counter sticks at UINT32_MAX instead of wrapping, so logging cannot start again. A third-party plugin that treats a failed EVENT_OBJECT_CALL registration as fatal now fails to load where it used to load and do nothing - that is intended and logged. With YYTK_HOOK_EXECUTEIT=1 the upstream behavior returns, including upstream's FWCodeEvent parameter-order mismatch (shared header says int, RValue*; the dispatched wrapper is RValue*, INT) - do not consume the event without fixing that first.

Log-markers: "ExecuteIt hook NOT installed by design"
Log-markers: "REFUSED EVENT_OBJECT_CALL"
Log-markers: "further refusals will not be logged"
Log-markers: "crash-report frames may be mislabelled Code_Execute"

Upstream-status: not submitted. Upstream v4.0.1 always installs the hook, treats a failed ExecuteIt lookup as fatal, and accepts every trigger in CreateCallback. The shared headers are untouched, so their CreateCallback comment does not list AURIE_UNAVAILABLE - the fork documentation has to.

diff --git a/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ObjectCallGateTest.cpp b/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ObjectCallGateTest.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c911f35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ObjectCallGateTest.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,240 @@
+// Host test for source/YYTK/Module Interface/ObjectCallGate.hpp - needs no game and no YYToolkit build.
+//
+// Build + run (x64 developer prompt, from the YYToolkit folder):
+//   cl /nologo /std:c++latest /EHsc /W4 hs-tests\ObjectCallGateTest.cpp && ObjectCallGateTest.exe
+//
+// Prints one line per check, and returns non-zero if any check failed.
+// Every predicate has a positive control (it says yes where it has to) and a
+// negative control (it says no where it has to), so a predicate that is stuck
+// at one answer can't pass.
+
+#include "../source/YYTK/Module Interface/ObjectCallGate.hpp"
+
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <thread>
+#include <vector>
+
+using namespace YYTK::ObjectCallGate;
+
+static int g_FailedChecks = 0;
+static int g_TotalChecks = 0;
+
+static void Check(
+	IN bool Condition,
+	IN const char* Description
+)
+{
+	g_TotalChecks++;
+	if (!Condition)
+		g_FailedChecks++;
+
+	printf("[%s] %s\n", Condition ? "PASS" : "FAIL", Description);
+}
+
+// What CreateCallback() does with one refused registration, minus the actual output.
+struct RefusalOutcome
+{
+	uint32_t Number = 0;
+	bool Logged = false;
+	bool LastLogged = false;
+};
+
+static RefusalOutcome RefuseOnce(
+	IN OUT std::atomic<uint32_t>& RefusalCount
+)
+{
+	RefusalOutcome outcome;
+	outcome.Number = CountRefusal(RefusalCount);
+	outcome.Logged = ShouldLogRefusal(outcome.Number);
+	outcome.LastLogged = outcome.Logged && IsLastLoggedRefusal(outcome.Number);
+	return outcome;
+}
+
+static void TestBuildSwitch()
+{
+	// The test is compiled without /DYYTK_HOOK_EXECUTEIT, so this is the shipped default.
+	Check(YYTK_HOOK_EXECUTEIT == 0, "switch: YYTK_HOOK_EXECUTEIT defaults to 0 (hook off)");
+	Check(max_logged_refusals == 8, "switch: at most 8 refusals are logged");
+}
+
+static void TestLimiterArithmetic()
+{
+	// Positive control: numbers 1..8 are logged.
+	bool first_eight_logged = true;
+	for (uint32_t number = 1; number <= 8; number++)
+		first_eight_logged = first_eight_logged && ShouldLogRefusal(number);
+	Check(first_eight_logged, "limiter+: refusals 1..8 are logged");
+
+	// Negative controls: 0 (no refusal), 9 and everything after it are silent.
+	Check(!ShouldLogRefusal(0), "limiter-: number 0 (no refusal happened) is not logged");
+	Check(!ShouldLogRefusal(9), "limiter-: refusal 9 is silent");
+	Check(!ShouldLogRefusal(10), "limiter-: refusal 10 is silent");
+	Check(!ShouldLogRefusal(1000000), "limiter-: refusal 1000000 is silent");
+	Check(!ShouldLogRefusal(UINT32_MAX), "limiter-: refusal UINT32_MAX is silent");
+
+	// The "further refusals are silent" suffix belongs to number 8, and to nothing else.
+	Check(IsLastLoggedRefusal(8), "last+: refusal 8 is the last logged one");
+	Check(!IsLastLoggedRefusal(7), "last-: refusal 7 is not the last logged one");
+	Check(!IsLastLoggedRefusal(9), "last-: refusal 9 is not the last logged one");
+	Check(!IsLastLoggedRefusal(0), "last-: number 0 is not the last logged one");
+	Check(!IsLastLoggedRefusal(1), "last-: refusal 1 is not the last logged one");
+}
+
+static void TestRefusalSequence()
+{
+	std::atomic<uint32_t> refusal_count = 0;
+
+	uint32_t logged = 0;
+	uint32_t last_logged = 0;
+	uint32_t last_logged_number = 0;
+	bool numbers_are_sequential = true;
+	bool every_call_was_counted = true;
+	bool logged_only_first_eight = true;
+
+	for (uint32_t call = 1; call <= 100; call++)
+	{
+		const RefusalOutcome outcome = RefuseOnce(refusal_count);
+
+		// A refusal is never turned into "not a refusal" by the limiter - number 0 means no refusal.
+		every_call_was_counted = every_call_was_counted && (outcome.Number != 0);
+		numbers_are_sequential = numbers_are_sequential && (outcome.Number == call);
+		logged_only_first_eight = logged_only_first_eight && (outcome.Logged == (call <= 8));
+
+		if (outcome.Logged)
+			logged++;
+
+		if (outcome.LastLogged)
+		{
+			last_logged++;
+			last_logged_number = outcome.Number;
+		}
+	}
+
+	Check(every_call_was_counted, "sequence+: all 100 refused registrations were counted as refusals");
+	Check(numbers_are_sequential, "sequence+: refusal numbers run 1, 2, 3, ...");
+	Check(refusal_count.load() == 100, "sequence+: the counter says 100 after 100 refusals");
+	Check(logged == 8, "sequence+: exactly 8 of 100 refusals were logged");
+	Check(logged_only_first_eight, "sequence-: calls 9..100 were silent, calls 1..8 were not");
+	Check(last_logged == 1 && last_logged_number == 8, "sequence+: exactly one refusal carries the 'further refusals' suffix, and it is number 8");
+}
+
+static void TestSaturation()
+{
+	// Positive control: just below the top, the counter still counts.
+	std::atomic<uint32_t> refusal_count = UINT32_MAX - 1;
+	const RefusalOutcome reaching_top = RefuseOnce(refusal_count);
+	Check(reaching_top.Number == UINT32_MAX && refusal_count.load() == UINT32_MAX, "saturation+: UINT32_MAX - 1 counts up to UINT32_MAX");
+	Check(!reaching_top.Logged, "saturation-: that refusal is silent");
+
+	// Negative control: at the top it must not wrap to 0, because 1..8 would be logged all over again.
+	bool stayed_silent = true;
+	for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++)
+	{
+		const RefusalOutcome outcome = RefuseOnce(refusal_count);
+		stayed_silent = stayed_silent && !outcome.Logged && !outcome.LastLogged && outcome.Number == UINT32_MAX;
+	}
+	Check(stayed_silent, "saturation-: 20 refusals at UINT32_MAX stay silent");
+	Check(refusal_count.load() == UINT32_MAX, "saturation-: the counter did not wrap around");
+}
+
+static void TestConcurrentRefusals()
+{
+	constexpr uint32_t thread_count = 4;
+	constexpr uint32_t refusals_per_thread = 5000;
+
+	std::atomic<uint32_t> refusal_count = 0;
+	std::atomic<uint32_t> logged = 0;
+	std::atomic<uint32_t> last_logged = 0;
+	std::atomic<uint32_t> silent = 0;
+
+	std::vector<std::thread> threads;
+	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < thread_count; i++)
+	{
+		threads.emplace_back(
+			[&]()
+			{
+				for (uint32_t call = 0; call < refusals_per_thread; call++)
+				{
+					const RefusalOutcome outcome = RefuseOnce(refusal_count);
+					if (outcome.Logged)
+						logged++;
+					else
+						silent++;
+					if (outcome.LastLogged)
+						last_logged++;
+				}
+			}
+		);
+	}
+
+	for (auto& thread : threads)
+		thread.join();
+
+	Check(refusal_count.load() == thread_count * refusals_per_thread, "threads+: 4 threads x 5000 refusals were all counted");
+	Check(logged.load() == 8, "threads+: exactly 8 refusals were logged across all threads");
+	Check(last_logged.load() == 1, "threads+: exactly one refusal carried the 'further refusals' suffix");
+	Check(silent.load() == thread_count * refusals_per_thread - 8, "threads-: the other 19992 refusals were silent");
+}
+
+static void TestNarrowImageName()
+{
+	// Positive controls
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"C:\\Games\\Hero Siege\\mods\\aurie\\ForgePact.dll") == "ForgePact.dll", "name+: only the file name is kept (backslashes)");
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"C:/Games/mods/aurie/Plugin.dll") == "Plugin.dll", "name+: only the file name is kept (forward slashes)");
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"Plugin.dll") == "Plugin.dll", "name+: a bare file name is kept as it is");
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"C:\\x\\100%s%n.dll") == "100%s%n.dll", "name+: percent signs survive (the name is an argument, never a format)");
+
+	// Negative controls
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"C:\\Users\\SomeUser\\mods\\Plugin.dll").find("SomeUser") == std::string::npos, "name-: the folder part (user profile) is dropped");
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"") == "<unknown>", "name-: an empty path is <unknown>");
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"C:\\mods\\") == "<unknown>", "name-: a path without a file name is <unknown>");
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"C:\\mods\\Eklenti\x015F\x0131.dll") == "Eklenti??.dll", "name-: non-ASCII characters become '?'");
+	Check(NarrowImageName(L"C:\\mods\\a\tb\n.dll") == "a?b?.dll", "name-: control characters become '?'");
+
+	const std::wstring long_name = L"C:\\mods\\" + std::wstring(500, L'A') + L".dll";
+	const std::string narrowed_long_name = NarrowImageName(long_name);
+	Check(narrowed_long_name.size() == max_image_name_length, "name-: an overlong name is cut to max_image_name_length");
+	Check(narrowed_long_name.ends_with("..."), "name-: a cut name ends in '...'");
+
+	const std::wstring exact_name = std::wstring(max_image_name_length, L'B');
+	Check(NarrowImageName(exact_name) == std::string(max_image_name_length, 'B'), "name+: a name of exactly max_image_name_length is not cut");
+}
+
+static void LocalRoutine()
+{
+}
+
+static void TestDescribeRoutineOwner()
+{
+	// Positive controls: a routine in this executable, and one in a system DLL.
+	const std::string own_name = DescribeRoutineOwner(reinterpret_cast<PVOID>(&LocalRoutine));
+	printf("       (own image reported as '%s')\n", own_name.c_str());
+	Check(own_name != "<unknown>" && own_name.ends_with(".exe"), "owner+: a routine in this executable is attributed to an .exe");
+	Check(own_name.find('\\') == std::string::npos && own_name.find('/') == std::string::npos, "owner+: the reported name carries no folder");
+
+	const HMODULE kernel32 = GetModuleHandleW(L"kernel32.dll");
+	const PVOID kernel32_routine = kernel32 ? reinterpret_cast<PVOID>(GetProcAddress(kernel32, "GetTickCount")) : nullptr;
+	const std::string kernel32_name = DescribeRoutineOwner(kernel32_routine);
+	printf("       (kernel32 routine reported as '%s')\n", kernel32_name.c_str());
+	Check(kernel32_routine != nullptr && _stricmp(kernel32_name.c_str(), "kernel32.dll") == 0, "owner+: a routine in kernel32 is attributed to kernel32.dll");
+
+	// Negative controls: addresses that are in no image at all.
+	int stack_variable = 0;
+	Check(DescribeRoutineOwner(nullptr) == "<unknown>", "owner-: nullptr is <unknown>");
+	Check(DescribeRoutineOwner(&stack_variable) == "<unknown>", "owner-: a stack address is <unknown>");
+	Check(DescribeRoutineOwner(reinterpret_cast<PVOID>(static_cast<uintptr_t>(0x10))) == "<unknown>", "owner-: an unmapped address is <unknown>");
+}
+
+int main()
+{
+	TestBuildSwitch();
+	TestLimiterArithmetic();
+	TestRefusalSequence();
+	TestSaturation();
+	TestConcurrentRefusals();
+	TestNarrowImageName();
+	TestDescribeRoutineOwner();
+
+	printf("%d checks, %d failed\n", g_TotalChecks, g_FailedChecks);
+	return g_FailedChecks == 0 ? 0 : 1;
+}
diff --git a/YYToolkit/source/YYTK/Module Interface/Interface.cpp b/YYToolkit/source/YYTK/Module Interface/Interface.cpp
index ce6d390..41e155a 100644
--- a/YYToolkit/source/YYTK/Module Interface/Interface.cpp	
+++ b/YYToolkit/source/YYTK/Module Interface/Interface.cpp	
@@ -1311,6 +1311,44 @@ namespace YYTK
 		IN int32_t Priority
 	)
 	{
+		// EVENT_OBJECT_CALL is only ever dispatched from Hooks::HkExecuteIt.
+		// If that hook isn't installed, the callback would be accepted here and then
+		// never be called - so refuse it, and put the name of whoever asked in the log.
+		if (Trigger == EVENT_OBJECT_CALL && !m_ObjectCallHookInstalled)
+		{
+			// Every refusal is counted, but only the first few are written out: each one is a
+			// flushed file write, and nothing stops a plugin from retrying the registration every frame.
+			const uint32_t refusal_number = ObjectCallGate::CountRefusal(m_ObjectCallRefusals);
+
+			if (ObjectCallGate::ShouldLogRefusal(refusal_number))
+			{
+				const std::string owner_name = ObjectCallGate::DescribeRoutineOwner(Routine);
+				const bool is_last_logged = ObjectCallGate::IsLastLoggedRefusal(refusal_number);
+
+				CmWriteLogOutput(
+					"[%s:%d] CreateCallback() => REFUSED EVENT_OBJECT_CALL from '%s' (module 0x%p, routine 0x%p), refusal %u: "
+					"the ExecuteIt hook is not installed in this build, so the callback would never be called. "
+					"Returning AURIE_UNAVAILABLE%s",
+					__FILE__,
+					__LINE__,
+					owner_name.c_str(),
+					Module,
+					Routine,
+					refusal_number,
+					is_last_logged ? " - further refusals will not be logged" : ""
+				);
+
+				CmWriteWarning(
+					"%s asked for EVENT_OBJECT_CALL, which this YYToolkit build does not provide (ExecuteIt is not hooked). "
+					"The callback was NOT registered.%s",
+					owner_name.c_str(),
+					is_last_logged ? " Further refusals will not be shown." : ""
+				);
+			}
+
+			return AURIE_UNAVAILABLE;
+		}
+
 		if (YkCallbackExists(Module, Routine))
 			return AURIE_OBJECT_ALREADY_EXISTS;
 
